# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored) for local development.
# Any string works locally; production uses a Worker secret.
RESPONSE_TOKEN_SECRET=local-development-secret-do-not-use-in-production

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT here: NOTIFIER, BETTER_AUTH_URL, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET,
# SIGNIN_ALLOWLIST, CANCEL_TOKEN_SECRET.
#
# Local sign-in needs all five, but this file is read by the Vitest workers
# pool as well as by `wrangler dev`, and it *overrides* the bindings
# vitest.config.ts sets explicitly. Adding SIGNIN_ALLOWLIST and
# BETTER_AUTH_URL here turned 56 server tests red at once: every signed-in
# test suddenly had a different allowlist and a different origin from the one
# it asserts against, so pages redirected instead of rendering.
#
# The browser suite therefore passes them to `wrangler dev` on the command
# line instead (see `DEV_VARS` in playwright.config.ts). To drive the app by
# hand with a working sign-in, use `npm run dev:browser`, which starts the
# dev server with the same values.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
